rticle's thesis, and the summary omits the central claim. A bounded repair_editorial_surfaces run is sufficient; no body edits are required.","requiredRepairs":["Regenerate the description and summary frontmatter surfaces from the admitted body via repair_editorial_surfaces; the current description is a procedural fact ('Neither FIFA nor New York City Department of Health officials immediately responded to Grist's request for comment') rather than an article summary, and the current summary jumps from scene-setting to NWSL policy contrast without stating the central thesis that FIFA lacks an air quality policy for wildfire smoke."],"repairTools":[{"tool":"repair_editorial_surfaces"}],"report":"## Source Adequacy\n\nThe packet carries one admitted source: a Grist.org article published 2026-07-17. The research intake flags that no current source has been established as a primary record (code: primary-source-unproven). For this manuscript's purpose â€” a secondary reporting synthesis that attributes every claim to the Grist article by inline citation â€” this limitation is handled correctly. The manuscript never asserts independent reporting, does not fabricate contact with FIFA or the NYC Department of Health, and correctly attributes the non-response record as Grist's request, not its own. The limitation does not rise to a source-layer failure.\n\n## Factual Claim Audit\n\nAll material claims in the body check against the Grist source summary:\n\n- World Cup final Sunday just outside New York City in an open-air stadium: **supported** (\"there's no way to close off the open-air stadium\").\n- Canadian wildfire smoke blanketing Midwest and East Coast: **supported** verbatim.\n- AQI reached \"unhealthy\" and \"very unhealthy\" Thursday, triggering state alert: **supported** (\"the state issued an alert as the air quality index climbed to 'unhealthy' and 'very unhealthy' levels\").\n- FIFA appears to have no standardized wildfire smoke policy: **supported** (\"FIFA does not appear to have any contingency plans in place for wildfire smoke\") â€” the manuscript correctly preserves the hedging word \"appears.\"\n- NWSL thresholds at AQI 101 and 200: **supported** with exact figures.\n- Neither FIFA nor NYC DoH responded to Grist's request: **supported** and correctly attributed to Grist's reporting, not this outlet's.\n- Dr. Courtney Howard quote with credentials and AP attribution: **supported** â€” Grist attributes it to AP; the manuscript passes through that attribution correctly.\n- Watanabe quote, title, and institution: **supported** exactly.\n- Friday morning conditions unhealthy near stadium, forecast to improve: **supported**.\n- Hazy, orange skies in NYC throughout the week: **supported**.\n\nNo claim is found to exceed what the source warrants. Modality is appropriately preserved throughout (\"appears,\" \"does not appear\").\n\n## Fairness and Institutional Response\n\nThe manuscript is critical of FIFA's preparedness. The fairness record is adequate for a secondary piece: FIFA's institutional position is represented via its previous statement about \"climate-related risks assessed as part of overall tournament planning,\" and the Grist non-response is acknowledged. No allegations of wrongdoing are made â€” the story reports an institutional gap, not misconduct. The Watanabe commentary is attributed with full credentials and is framed as his opinion, not fact.\n\n## Headline and Lede Faithfulness\n\nHeadline (\"FIFA Lacks Air Quality Policy as Wildfire Smoke Approaches World Cup Final\") accurately captures the thesis with appropriate present-tense scope. \"Lacks\" is supported by \"does not appear to have any contingency plans\" â€” a reasonable editorial condensation that does not over-assert. The lede paragraph correctly establishes the match, the venue type, and the atmospheric threat before the body develops the policy gap. No forbidden strengthenings are present.\n\n## Near-Duplicate Proximity Warnings\n\nThe deterministic gate flagged eleven near-duplicate-proximity pairs. Reviewing the actual prose: the flagged sentences share contextual framing (same event, same week, same geography) rather than genuine semantic repetition. Each sentence conveys a distinct fact â€” the match venue, the geographic scope of smoke, Thursday's AQI event, the FIFA policy absence, the NWSL contrast, the non-response, the physician quote, the vulnerable-groups caveat, the Friday forecast, the forecast uncertainty, and the Watanabe close. None repeat substantive information. These are algorithmic proximity detections, not editorial defects. No body edits are warranted on this basis.\n\n## Frontmatter Defects â€” Description and Summary\n\nThis is where the writer-model failed.\n\n**Description:** \"Neither FIFA nor New York City Department of Health officials immediately responded to Grist's request for comment.\" This is a single procedural fact drawn from the body, not a summary of the article's argument. A description surface should convey the piece's central claim and scope to external readers and search engines. Using the no-response line as the description misrepresents the article's purpose and wastes the SEO and discovery surface.\n\n**Summary:** \"As the World Cup final approaches this Sunday just outside New York City, atmospheric conditions have cast uncertainty over the match, which is slated to be held in an open-air stadium. By contrast, the National Women's Soccer League maintains a detailed policy that mandates game modifications or postponements when the air quality index reaches specific thresholds, such as 101 or 200.\" The summary opens with scene-setting and closes with the NWSL contrast but never states the central thesis â€” that FIFA has no air quality policy â€” in the summary block. A reader encountering only this summary cannot determine what the article argues. The abrupt pivot to NWSL without establishing FIFA's gap makes the summary incoherent in isolation.\n\nBoth surfaces should be regenerated from the admitted body via repair_editorial_surfaces. The body is factually sound and the deterministic projection should produce coherent, thesis-first surfaces.\n\n## Pipeline Diagnosis\n\nThe failure is confined to the writer-model's frontmatter surface projection. The body, attribution, sourcing, and headline layers are all acceptable. The defect does not require body edits or assignment replay. A single repair_editorial_surfaces pass is the bounded and sufficient correction."}ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;GGQVE9CI2WgDNFSAYZaAFr6Hb-nw9NuIGO7RMVhCjEAƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx$d5b4344f-0137-4d38-a701-a442ebbfeaf9ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;op3KKC1WonoFSoBn2EewPQEJLDdaHTwpF7bRF2oFBRQƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkhtool_useƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;dkhRVpoFSeI6UwQbXrQ_E3jwkIiEL5m99q43eMP3_Xwƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;dU56fwc1Wpo7ohxNTiJdZ6n3XDoePmFXOUY0-K4b5v8ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarklwriter-modelƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;f4tV1InRQXxH9T_Jt0h7Wr2wDbLQ6Avl31Er1zgFB3Mƒdpairƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;KSWxdCtFbMyn8gNNBFmEmt-KTQTV3oD6Mew0-AccMs4ƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;Sa82oTntL2JaYpWg5sTqDY-zn7lD_Gylj-EJ_122Lucƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxrepair_editorial_surfacesƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;lj-vYmkUW77mpceIIrlaCYxdNwuod16fPg16MRWRWwYƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxAwriter-model: draft generation â€” frontmatter surface projectionƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;amWy7WP2pqoPAc3JJJFs_fVEOErNI82xSrD5ceQHe3gƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkyh## Source Adequacy

The packet carries one admitted source: a Grist.org article published 2026-07-17. The research intake flags that no current source has been established as a primary record (code: primary-source-unproven). For this manuscript's purpose â€” a secondary reporting synthesis that attributes every claim to the Grist article by inline citation â€” this limitation is handled correctly. The manuscript never asserts independent reporting, does not fabricate contact with FIFA or the NYC Department of Health, and correctly attributes the non-response record as Grist's request, not its own. The limitation does not rise to a source-layer failure.

## Factual Claim Audit

All material claims in the body check against the Grist source summary:

- World Cup final Sunday just outside New York City in an open-air stadium: **supported** ("there's no way to close off the open-air stadium").
- Canadian wildfire smoke blanketing Midwest and East Coast: **supported** verbatim.
- AQI reached "unhealthy" and "very unhealthy" Thursday, triggering state alert: **supported** ("the state issued an alert as the air quality index climbed to 'unhealthy' and 'very unhealthy' levels").
- FIFA appears to have no standardized wildfire smoke policy: **supported** ("FIFA does not appear to have any contingency plans in place for wildfire smoke") â€” the manuscript correctly preserves the hedging word "appears."
- NWSL thresholds at AQI 101 and 200: **supported** with exact figures.
- Neither FIFA nor NYC DoH responded to Grist's request: **supported** and correctly attributed to Grist's reporting, not this outlet's.
- Dr. Courtney Howard quote with credentials and AP attribution: **supported** â€” Grist attributes it to AP; the manuscript passes through that attribution correctly.
- Watanabe quote, title, and institution: **supported** exactly.
- Friday morning conditions unhealthy near stadium, forecast to improve: **supported**.
- Hazy, orange skies in NYC throughout the week: **supported**.

No claim is found to exceed what the source warrants. Modality is appropriately preserved throughout ("appears," "does not appear").

## Fairness and Institutional Response

The manuscript is critical of FIFA's preparedness. The fairness record is adequate for a secondary piece: FIFA's institutional position is represented via its previous statement about "climate-related risks assessed as part of overall tournament planning," and the Grist non-response is acknowledged. No allegations of wrongdoing are made â€” the story reports an institutional gap, not misconduct. The Watanabe commentary is attributed with full credentials and is framed as his opinion, not fact.

## Headline and Lede Faithfulness

Headline ("FIFA Lacks Air Quality Policy as Wildfire Smoke Approaches World Cup Final") accurately captures the thesis with appropriate present-tense scope. "Lacks" is supported by "does not appear to have any contingency plans" â€” a reasonable editorial condensation that does not over-assert. The lede paragraph correctly establishes the match, the venue type, and the atmospheric threat before the body develops the policy gap. No forbidden strengthenings are present.

## Near-Duplicate Proximity Warnings

The deterministic gate flagged eleven near-duplicate-proximity pairs. Reviewing the actual prose: the flagged sentences share contextual framing (same event, same week, same geography) rather than genuine semantic repetition. Each sentence conveys a distinct fact â€” the match venue, the geographic scope of smoke, Thursday's AQI event, the FIFA policy absence, the NWSL contrast, the non-response, the physician quote, the vulnerable-groups caveat, the Friday forecast, the forecast uncertainty, and the Watanabe close. None repeat substantive information. These are algorithmic proximity detections, not editorial defects. No body edits are warranted on this basis.

## Frontmatter Defects â€” Description and Summary

This is where the writer-model failed.

**Description:** "Neither FIFA nor New York City Department of Health officials immediately responded to Grist's request for comment." This is a single procedural fact drawn from the body, not a summary of the article's argument. A description surface should convey the piece's central claim and scope to external readers and search engines. Using the no-response line as the description misrepresents the article's purpose and wastes the SEO and discovery surface.

**Summary:** "As the World Cup final approaches this Sunday just outside New York City, atmospheric conditions have cast uncertainty over the match, which is slated to be held in an open-air stadium. By contrast, the National Women's Soccer League maintains a detailed policy that mandates game modifications or postponements when the air quality index reaches specific thresholds, such as 101 or 200." The summary opens with scene-setting and closes with the NWSL contrast but never states the central thesis â€” that FIFA has no air quality policy â€” in the summary block. A reader encountering only this summary cannot determine what the article argues. The abrupt pivot to NWSL without establishing FIFA's gap makes the summary incoherent in isolation.

Both surfaces should be regenerated from the admitted body via repair_editorial_surfaces. The body is factually sound and the deterministic projection should produce coherent, thesis-first surfaces.

## Pipeline Diagnosis

